    "reading": "The turn is not buying distance. It swaps which arm stands where: the nests are on the tool arm's side of the centre line, and the picking arm is on the other. Standing still, the picking arm has to reach across the tool arm. Turning puts the picking arm over the nests and moves the tool arm clear.",
